In Elasticsearch, "search after" is a pagination method that allows you to retrieve the next page of search results by specifying the value of the last document in the previous page. This feature can be useful when working with large result sets, as it can improve performance and reduce the amount of memory used to hold search results.

In .NET Core, you can use the Elasticsearch.Net and NEST packages to connect to an Elasticsearch cluster and perform search after queries. Here's an example of how you might implement search after pagination:

```csharp
using Nest;

