Creating a simple bookkeeping application for a self-employed individual in Switzerland can be achieved using a combination of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. In this example, I will show you how to create a JavaScript slider for income and expenses.

First, let's create the HTML structure for our sliders:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Simple Bookkeeping</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>Simple Bookkeeping for Self-employed in Switzerland</h1>

        <div class="slider-container">
            <h2>Income</h2>
            <input type="range" min="0" max="100000" value="0" class="slider" id="income-slider">
            <p>Amount: <span id="income-value">0</span> CHF</p>
        </div>

        <div class="slider-container">
            <h2>Expenses</h2>
            <input type="range" min="0" max="100000" value="0" class="slider" id="expenses-slider">
            <p>Amount: <span id="expenses-value">0</span> CHF</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

Next, we'll create a simple CSS file (styles.css) for styling:

```css
body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    text-align: center;
}

.container {
    width: 80%;
    margin: 0 auto;
}

.slider-container {
    margin: 20px 0;
}

.slider {
    width: 100%;
}
```

Finally, we'll create a JavaScript file (script.js) that connects the sliders to their respective display value elements:

```javascript
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
    const incomeSlider = document.getElementById('income-slider');
    const incomeValue = document.getElementById('income-value');
    const expensesSlider = document.getElementById('expenses-slider');
    const expensesValue = document.getElementById('expenses-value');

    incomeSlider.addEventListener('input', function() {
        incomeValue.innerHTML = this.value;
    });

    expensesSlider.addEventListener('input', function() {
        expensesValue.innerHTML = this.value;
    });
});
```

These files will create a simple bookkeeping application with sliders for income and expenses that display the values in Swiss Francs (CHF). Ensure that the HTML, CSS, and JavaScript files are in the same directory and open the HTML file in a web browser to see the application in action.

