1. Create a new 2D Sprite Shape object in your Unity scene.
2. Replace the default Sprite Shape profile with your own if necessary.
3. Make sure your object has a Sprite Shape Controller component.
4. Add this updated TerrainCreator script to your Sprite Shape object.
5. You can adjust the `scale`, `numofPoints`, `heightScale`, and `perlinOffset` in the inspector to modify the terrain generation as needed.

