1. Install IntelliJ IDEA and set up a Kotlin project
2. Open build.gradle file and add the following libraries to the dependencies:

```groovy
dependencies {
    implementation "org.jetbrains.kotlin:kotlin-stdlib:$kotlin_version"
    implementation 'com.squareup.okhttp3:okhttp:4.9.2'
    implementation 'com.squareup.moshi:moshi-kotlin:1.12.0'
}
```

The above dependencies include OKHttp for making network calls and Moshi for parsing JSON data.

3. Create a file named `ApiService.kt` containing the utility functions for fetching data from the GitHub API:

```kotlin
import okhttp3.OkHttpClient
import okhttp3.Request
import java.io.IOException

object ApiService {
    private const val BASE_URL = "https://api.github.com"
    private const val HEADER_AUTH = "Authorization"

    private val client = OkHttpClient()

    @Throws(IOException::class)
    fun getFavoriteUser(username: String, token: String): String {
        val request = Request.Builder()
            .url("$BASE_URL/users/$username")
            .header(HEADER_AUTH, "token $token")
            .build()

        client.newCall(request).execute().use { response ->
            if (!response.isSuccessful) throw IOException("Unexpected code $response")

            return response.body!!.string()
        }
    }
}
```

Replace `token` with your personal access token, create one by following the GitHub documentation: https://docs.github.com/en/authentication/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure/creating-a-personal-access-token

