To update the currency balance live, you can use a coroutine that periodically checks the player's balance and updates the UI accordingly. Unity's coroutines allow you to repeat a task in a non-blocking manner, which is suitable for real-time updates.

Here's how you can modify your code to update the currencies live:

1. Replace your existing `LoadAllCurrencies` method by starting a coroutine named `UpdateCurrencyBalance`.

```csharp
public void LoadAllCurrencies()
{
    StartCoroutine(UpdateCurrencyBalance());
}
```

2. Implement the `UpdateCurrencyBalance` coroutine that periodically checks and updates the player's balance.

```csharp
private IEnumerator UpdateCurrencyBalance() 
{
    while (true)
    {
        List<CurrencyDefinition> definitions = await EconomyService.Instance.Configuration.GetCurrenciesAsync();

        // Set up tasks to query balances for both FOX_COIN and FANTASY_DIAMOND
        Task<PlayerBalance> softCurrencyTask = null;
        Task<PlayerBalance> premiumCurrencyTask = null;

        foreach (CurrencyDefinition currency in definitions)
        {
            if (currency.Id.ToString() == "FOX_COIN")
            {
                softCurrencyTask = currency.GetPlayerBalanceAsync();
            }
            else if (currency.Id.ToString() == "FANTASY_DIAMOND")
            {
                premiumCurrencyTask = currency.GetPlayerBalanceAsync();
            }
        }

        // Wait for both balance queries to complete
        await Task.WhenAll(softCurrencyTask, premiumCurrencyTask);

        // Update the UI with the balances
        if (softCurrencyTask != null)
        {
            softCurrency.text = softCurrencyTask.Result.Balance.ToString();
        }
        if (premiumCurrencyTask != null)
        {
            premiumCurrency.text = premiumCurrencyTask.Result.Balance.ToString();
        }

        // Wait for a time interval before checking the balance again
        yield return new WaitForSeconds(5); // Customize this value to set the desired update frequency (in seconds)
    }
}
```

Now, the currency balances will automatically update every 5 seconds (or the time interval you set). You can adjust the update interval by changing the value of `WaitForSeconds` in the `UpdateCurrencyBalance` coroutine. Also, make sure to import the necessary namespaces for the coroutine:

```csharp
using System.Collections;
using System.Collections.Generic;
// Other necessary imports
```

This approach will update the currency balance periodically. If you want the balance to update only when a specific event occurs (e.g., a purchase is made), you can call the `LoadAllCurrencies()` method from the corresponding event handler function.

