La función proporcionada se encarga de crear o actualizar un camping con sus alojamientos y unidades asociadas.

Aquí hay una versión optimizada y simplificada de la función, manteniendo la funcionalidad original:

```javascript
campingController.createCamping = async (req, res, next) => {
  delete req.body.owner;

  const session = await mongoose.startSession();
  session.startTransaction();

  let camping;

  try {
    if (req.body._id) {
      camping = await Camping.findById(req.body._id);
      if (!camping.owner.equals(req.user._id)) {
        return next(new Unauthorized())
      }
    } else {
      delete req.body._id;
      camping = new Camping({ ...req.body, owner: req.user._id });
    }

    const campingLodgingsOperations = req.body.lodgings.flatMap((lodging) => {
      if (!lodging._id || lodging._id.startsWith('new')) {
        lodging.camping = camping._id;
        delete lodging._id;
      } else if (!camping._id.equals(lodging.camping)) {
        return next(new Unauthorized())
      }

      const lodgingOperation = lodging._id
        ? { updateOne: { filter: { _id: lodging._id }, update: { $set: lodging } } }
        : { insertOne: { document: lodging } };

      const unitOperations = lodging.units.map((unit) => {
        if (!unit._id || unit._id.startsWith('new')) {
          unit.campingLodging = lodging._id;
          delete unit._id;
        } else if (lodging._id !== unit.lodging) {
          return next(new Unauthorized());
        }

        return unit._id
          ? { updateOne: { filter: { _id: unit._id }, update: { $set: unit } } }
          : { insertOne: { document: unit } };
      });

      return [lodgingOperation, ...unitOperations];
    });

    await CampingLodging.bulkWrite(campingLodgingsOperations, { session });
    await CampingUnit.bulkWrite(campingUnitsOperations, { session });

    const response = await camping.save();

    await session.commitTransaction();
    res.status(201).json({
      message: "Camping created successfully",
      camping: response
    });
  } catch (error) {
    await session.abortTransaction();
    return next(error);
  }
  session.endSession();
};
```

En resumen, se ha sustituido el uso de `for` por métodos funcionales como `flatMap` y `map` para reducir la complejidad y el tamaño del código. Además, se ha eliminado el uso redundante de variables `campingLodgingsOperations` y `campingUnitsOperations`.

To keep the DatePicker open while selecting multiple dates, you can create a custom DatePicker skin that allows multiple date selection and hack the default behavior of DatePicker closing upon selecting a date.

Here's a sample code that illustrates how this can be done:

```java
import javafx.application.Application;
import javafx.beans.property.ObjectProperty;
import javafx.beans.property.SimpleObjectProperty;
import javafx.collections.FXCollections;
import javafx.scene.Scene;
import javafx.scene.control.DateCell;
import javafx.scene.control.DatePicker;
import javafx.scene.control.Skin;
import javafx.scene.layout.VBox;
import javafx.stage.Stage;
import javafx.util.Callback;

import java.time.LocalDate;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public class MultipleDatePicker extends Application {

    @Override
    public void start(Stage primaryStage) {
        VBox root = new VBox();
        Scene scene = new Scene(root, 300, 250);

        DatePicker datePicker = new MultipleDatePicker();

        root.getChildren().add(datePicker);

        primaryStage.setScene(scene);
        primaryStage.show();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        launch(args);
    }

    public static class MultipleDatePicker extends DatePicker {

        // Property to store selected multiple dates
        private final ObjectProperty<List<LocalDate>> selectedDates;

        public MultipleDatePicker() {
            super();
            selectedDates = new SimpleObjectProperty<>(new ArrayList<>());
            this.setSkin(new MultipleDateSkin(this));
            this.selectedDates.setValue(FXCollections.observableArrayList());
        }

        public final ObjectProperty<List<LocalDate>> selectedDatesProperty() {
            return selectedDates;
        }

        public final void setSelectedDates(List<LocalDate> value) {
            selectedDates.set(value);
        }

        public final List<LocalDate> getSelectedDates() {
            return selectedDates.get();
        }
    }

    public static class MultipleDateSkin extends DatePickerSkin {

        private DatePicker datePicker;

        public MultipleDateSkin(DatePicker control) {
            super(control);
            datePicker = control;
            updateDayCellFactory();
        }

        private void updateDayCellFactory() {
            datePicker.setDayCellFactory(new Callback<DatePicker, DateCell>() {
                @Override
                public DateCell call(DatePicker param) {
                    return new DateCell() {

                        @Override
                        public void updateItem(LocalDate item, boolean empty) {
                            super.updateItem(item, empty);
                            LocalDate value = datePicker.getValue();

                            if (value != null && datePicker.getSelectedDates().contains(item)) {
                                getStyleClass().add("selected");
                            } else {
                                getStyleClass().remove("selected");
                            }
                        }
                    };
                }
            });
        }

        @Override
        protected void handleControlPropertyChanged(String p) {
            super.handleControlPropertyChanged(p);
            if ("DAY_CELL_FACTORY".equals(p)) {
                return;
            }
            if ("SHOW_WEEK_NUMBERS".equals(p)) {
                return;
            }
            if (p.equals("CALENDAR_VALUE")) {
                LocalDate date = datePicker.getValue();
                if (date != null) {
                    boolean isSelected = datePicker.getSelectedDates().contains(date);
                    if (isSelected) {
                        datePicker.getSelectedDates().remove(date);
                    } else {
                        datePicker.getSelectedDates().add(date);
                    }
                    datePicker.setValue(null);
                }
            }
        }

        @Override
        public Node getPopupContent() {
            Node popupContent = super.getPopupContent();

            if (popupContent instanceof VBox) {
                VBox datePane = (VBox) popupContent;
                datePane.addEventFilter(MouseEvent.MOUSE_PRESSED, event -> event.consume());
            }

            return popupContent;
        }
    }
}
```

In this example, we create a custom `MultipleDatePicker` that extends `DatePicker` and `MultipleDateSkin` that extends `DatePickerSkin`. We've implemented the code for selection and deselection of dates and made it so that it consumes the mouse press events with the `event.consume()` function, keeping the DatePicker open when selecting multiple dates.

To enable multiple date selection and style the selected dates, go to your project's styles.css file and add:

```css
