    template<typename U1, typename U2, typename U3>
    ThreeMemberClass(U1 value1, U2 value2, U3 value3) : first(value1), second(value2), third(value3) {}

    template<typename U1 = T1>
    U1& getFirst() { return first; }

    template<typename U2 = T2>
    U2& getSecond() { return second; }

    template<typename U3 = T3>
    U3& getThird() { return third; }

private:
    T1 first;
    T2 second;
    T3 third;
};
```

In this implementation, the class has three template arguments `T1`, `T2`, and `T3` that default to `void`. This allows the class to be instantiated with any number of template arguments.

The class also provides four constructors that can be used to initialize the members of the class. The first constructor initializes no members, the second initializes the first member, the third initializes the first two members, and the fourth initializes all three members.

The `getFirst()`, `getSecond()`, and `getThird()` member functions are also template functions that return a reference to the corresponding member of the class.

