To do this, you can add a new state variable `isAmountManuallyUpdated` and set it to `true` when the user manually updates the amount field. Then, check this flag in your side effect and only update the amount when the flag is `false`.

Here's how you can implement this in your `AmountField` component:

1. Add a new state variable `isAmountManuallyUpdated` and set it initially to `false`.

```javascript
const [isAmountManuallyUpdated, setIsAmountManuallyUpdated] = React.useState(false);
```

2. Set this flag to `true` when the user manually updates the amount field.

```javascript
const handleChange = (moneyValue: string | null) => {
  // ...
  setIsAmountManuallyUpdated(true);
  // ...
};
```

3. Reset this flag to `false` if needed, for example, when the checkbox is checked, so that the side effect can be executed again.

In your side effect for updating the amount, add a condition to check the `isAmountManuallyUpdated` flag, and only update the amount when the flag is `false`:

```javascript
if (isAmountManuallyUpdated === false) {
  // update the amount only if it wasn't manually updated
} else {
  //skip updating the amount as it was manually updated
}
```

With this implementation, the side effect will be skipped if the amount is manually updated, and it will be executed if the amount is not manually updated.

