This function checks if the user has scrolled down more than a quarter of the screen height. If so, it adds the "navbar-sticky" class to the navbar and the "theme-switcher-show" class to the theme-switcher button. If not, it removes those classes.

The `updateNavbar` function is called whenever the user scrolls, as seen in the following event listener:

