We then define a POST endpoint with `app.post()`. Inside this endpoint's callback function, we log the data that the client sends in the request body using `console.log()`. We also send a simple response to inform the client that the server has received the request and displayed the data.

Finally, we tell the app to listen on port 3000 for incoming requests using `app.listen()`. When the server is ready to receive requests, we log a message to the server console.

