To read data from a Google Sheet using Google Apps Script, you can follow the example below. This script will log the content of the sheet in the console, you can change it to return the values instead, or write it to another sheet, or process the data in another way.

```javascript
function readDataFromSheet() {
  // Change to the ID of the Google Sheet you want to work with.
  var sheetId = 'your_spreadsheet_id';

  // Open the Google Sheet by ID
  var ss = SpreadsheetApp.openById(sheetId);

  // Access the first sheet in the spreadsheet
  var sheet = ss.getSheets()[0];

  // Get the data range of the sheet, which is the occupied cells
  var range = sheet.getDataRange();

  // Get values of cells in the data range
  var values = range.getValues();

  // Log the content of the sheet to the console
  for (var i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {
    console.log(values[i]);
  }
}
```

