Creating an endless runner game in Phaser requires a substantial amount of code and cannot be provided in a short answer format. However, I can give you an outline and the basic structure of how to create an endless runner game in Phaser using separate JavaScript files.

1. First, create the following files: index.html, menu.js, main.js, game.js, and preload.js.

2. In the index.html file, add the following code to set up the basic structure and include Phaser:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
    <head>
        <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/phaser/2.6.2/phaser.js"></script>
        <script src="preload.js"></script>
        <script src="menu.js"></script>
        <script src="main.js"></script>
        <script src="game.js"></script>
    </head>
    <body>
        <script type="text/javascript">
            window.onload = function () {
                var game = new Phaser.Game(800, 600, Phaser.AUTO, '');

                game.state.add('Preload', Preload);
                game.state.add('Menu', Menu);
                game.state.add('Game', Game);

                game.state.start('Preload');
            };
        </script>
    </body>
</html>
```

3. In the preload.js file, add the following code to load your assets (you will need to replace 'path/to/asset' with the actual file paths):

```javascript
var Preload = {
    preload: function() {
        // Load assets
        this.load.image('player', 'path/to/player_asset');
        this.load.image('ground', 'path/to/ground_asset');
        this.load.image('obstacle', 'path/to/obstacle_asset');
    },

    create: function() {
        this.state.start('Menu');
    }
};
```

4. In the menu.js file, add the following code to create a simple menu:

```javascript
var Menu = {
    create: function() {
        // Add menu text
        var menuText = this.add.text(this.world.centerX, this.world.centerY, 'Press Any Key to Start', { font: '24px Arial', fill: '#fff', align: 'center' });
        menuText.anchor.set(0.5);

        // Start the game when a key is pressed
        this.input.onDown.addOnce(() => this.state.start('Game'), this);
    }
};
```

5. In the game.js file, create the main game logic:

```javascript
var Game = {
    create: function() {
        // Create the player, ground, and obstacles here
    },

    update: function() {
        // Update the game loop with the logic for the endless runner
    },

    gameOver: function() {
        // Restart the game or return to the menu
    }
};
```

6. You'll then need to create the endless runner game logic by updating the 'create' and 'update' functions in the game.js file according to your desired game behavior.

7. Remember to add your actual assets and modify the paths in the preload.js file.

