To use cookies in Pinia with Vue 3, you can create a new store module to encapsulate cookie-related logic. 

1. Install cookie-parser: The easiest way to handle cookies in Pinia is by using the `cookie-parser` package. To install it, simply run `npm install cookie-parser`.

2. Create a store module: Create a new store module by using the `defineStore` method from Pinia. The store module will contain methods to set, get, and delete cookies. 

```javascript
import { defineStore } from "pinia";
import cookieParser from "cookie-parser";

const cookieStore = defineStore({
  id: "cookie",
  state: () => ({
    cookies: cookieParser(),
  }),
  actions: {
    setCookie(key, value, options) {
      this.cookies[key] = value;
      document.cookie = `${key}=${value}; ${
        options ? options : "SameSite=Lax"
      }`;
    },
    getCookie(key) {
      return this.cookies[key];
    },
    removeCookie(key) {
      delete this.cookies[key];
      document.cookie = `${key}=; expires=Thu, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 UTC; SameSite=Lax`;
    },
  },
});

export default cookieStore;
