void OnRep_TimerValue();

virtual void GetLifetimeReplicatedProps(TArray<FLifetimeProperty>& OutLifetimeProps) const override;

// In your source file: Sync timer value from the server to the clients
void AMyActor::OnRep_TimerValue()
{
    // The timer value has been updated on a client, so update the UI here as needed.
}

// Replicate the timer value
void AMyActor::GetLifetimeReplicatedProps(TArray<FLifetimeProperty>& OutLifetimeProps) const
{
    Super::GetLifetimeReplicatedProps(OutLifetimeProps);

    DOREPLIFETIME(AMyActor, TimerValue);
}
```

By using this approach, you can ensure clients have a responsive and smooth UI experience, and you maintain the correct timer value across all clients by keeping the server as the definitive source.

Keep in mind this example assumes you are using an `AActor`-based class (`AMyActor`). If you are working with a different class, make sure to adjust the replicated properties according to the class you are working with.

