Golang 语言使用 Goroutines 和 Channels 进行并发编程，而不是使用传统的线程和进程。在 Golang 中，Goroutines 类似于轻量级线程，而 Channels 用于在 Goroutines 之间传递数据。这里有一个简单的例子来说明它们是如何工作的：

```go
package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"sync"
)

func main() {
	wg := &sync.WaitGroup{}
	ch := make(chan string)

	// 启动 3 个 Goroutine 来处理任务
	for i := 0; i < 3; i++ {
		wg.Add(1)
		go func(id int, ch chan string, wg *sync.WaitGroup) {
			defer wg.Done()
			msg := fmt.Sprintf("Goroutine %d finished processing", id)
			ch <- msg
		}(i, ch, wg)
	}

	// 在单独的 Goroutine 中接收通道消息
	go func(ch chan string) {
		for msg := range ch {
			fmt.Println(msg)
		}
	}(ch)

	wg.Wait()
	close(ch)
}
```

上面的代码会创建 3 个 Goroutines，它们会并发执行。每个 Goroutine 都会在完成任务后将一条消息发送到通道 (channel)。`main` 函数中的另一个 Goroutine 负责从通道 (channel) 中接收和打印这些消息。

需要注意的是，Golang 并原生支持线程和进程的概念。提到线程和进程区别，通常是从资源开销、内存、通信等方面进行比较。在 Golang 中，Goroutines 类似于轻量级线程，提供了更高效、简单的方式处理并发。所创建的基本上是用户空间的线程（非系统线程），由 Go 语言运行时进行调度，但最终底层依然会使用操作系统的线程。

You can use recursion to find unique Fibonacci numbers that add up to a given number. Here, I am giving you an example of the C code that might be helpful for you:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int largest_fibonacci(int num) {
  int fib1 = 1;
  int fib2 = 1;
  int fib = fib1 + fib2;

  while (fib <= num) {
    fib1 = fib2;
    fib2 = fib;
    fib = fib1 + fib2;
  }

  return fib2;
}

void decompose_into_fibs(int num) {
  if (num <= 0) {
    return;
  }

  int largest_fib = largest_fibonacci(num);
  printf("%d ", largest_fib);

  decompose_into_fibs(num - largest_fib);
}

int main() {
  int num;

  // Read the user input
  printf("Enter a number: ");
  scanf("%d", &num);

  // Decompose the number into unique Fibonacci numbers
  printf("Decomposed Fibonacci numbers: ");
  decompose_into_fibs(num);
  printf("\n");

  return 0;
}
```
In this code, we first find the largest Fibonacci number less than or equal to the given number. Then, we subtract that Fibonacci number from the number and repeat the process with the remaining value. The process continues until the remaining value becomes zero.

Este é um projeto interessante em que sistemas de blocos colidem de maneira elástica e você deseja obter o número π com base nas colisões. Vou te mostrar uma maneira de abordar esse problema e escrever um programa em C.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <math.h>

typedef struct {
    double x;
    double v;
    double mass;
} Block;

int collide(Block *block1, Block *block2) {
    if ((block1->v < 0 && block2->v < 0) || (block1->v <= block2->v)) return 0;

    double rel_v = (block2->v - block1->v) / (block1->mass + block2->mass);

    block1->v += 2 * block2->mass * rel_v;
    block2->v -= 2 * block1->mass * rel_v;

    return 1;
}

int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    Block blocks[4];
    double simulation_time;

    for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
        scanf("%lf %lf %lf", &blocks[i].x, &blocks[i].v, &blocks[i].mass);
    }

    scanf("%lf", &simulation_time);

    long collisions[3] = {0, 0, 0};

    while (1) {
        int min_index = -1;
        double min_time = simulation_time;

        for (int i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
            if (blocks[i].v >= blocks[i + 1].v) continue;

            double t = (blocks[i + 1].x - blocks[i].x) / (blocks[i].v - blocks[i + 1].v);

            if (t < min_time) {
                min_time = t;
                min_index = i;
            }
        }

        if (min_index == -1) {
            break;
        }

        for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
            blocks[i].x += blocks[i].v * min_time;
        }

        collide(&blocks[min_index], &blocks[min_index + 1]);
        ++collisions[min_index];
    }

    printf("Numero de colisoes por bloco: %ld %ld %ld\n", collisions[0], collisions[1], collisions[2]);
    printf("Numero total de colisoes: %ld\n", collisions[0] + collisions[1] + collisions[2]);
    printf("Colisoes dos dois blocos a direita: %ld\n", collisions[1] + collisions[2]);

    simulation_time -= fmod(simulation_time, 0.1);

    for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
        blocks[i].x += blocks[i].v * simulation_time;
        printf("x%d = %.6lf v%d = %.6lf d%d = %.6lf\n", i, blocks[i].x, i, blocks[i].v, i, blocks[i].x - (0.1 * i));
    }

    printf("Nao ha mais colisoes\n");

    return 0;
}
```

Este programa em C implementa a simulação de blocos colidindo elasticamente e calcula o número total de colisões, incluindo colisões entre os dois blocos à direita. Agora você pode testar esse código com os arquivos de entrada fornecidos no enunciado e verificar se os resultados são os esperados.

