We've updated the `RedisSegmentRepository.GetBySessionAndRefNum()` method to check for expired segments in Redis and if expired, search for the segment in MongoDB. It first searches for expired segments in MongoDB, and if found, returns them since their expiration time can still be within the catch-up period. If not found, it returns an error.

