        // double the points if the joker was not used in this category
        if (category_multiplier == 1 && category_questions > 0) {
            category_points *= 2;
        }

        // add bonus points for questions after the boundary
        if (category_questions >= boundary) {
            category_points += (category_questions - boundary) * 2;
        }

        // add category points to the total and halftime points
        total_points += category_points * category_multiplier;
        if (category_multiplier == 1) {
            halftime_points += category_points;
        } else {
            halftime_points += category_points / 2;
        }

        // print answers for this category
        for (int i = 0; i < category_questions; i++) {
            printf("%c", answer);
        }
        printf("\n");
    } while (answer != EOF);

    // print total and halftime points in the desired format
    printf("%d %d\n", halftime_points, total_points);

    return 0;
}
```

The code reads the boundary value from the user and then enters a loop that reads the answer information for each category until the end of input is reached. For each category, it counts the number of correct answers, applies the multiplier for the '$' symbol (if present), adds bonus points for questions worth 2 points, and doubles the points earned in the category (if applicable). It then adds the category points to the total points, and prints the answer information for the category. After all categories have been processed, the program prints the number of halftime and total points in the desired format.

Note that the code assumes that the categories are separated by newline characters. It also assumes that there is no input validation needed for the answer information (e.g., the number of answers per category is not checked, and any input that is not '-', 'o', 'x', '$', or whitespace is treated as an ignored character). You may need to modify the code if some of these assumptions do not hold in your use case.

In order to load elements into a WPF app using a `config.json` file, you need to perform the following steps:

