1. Define the geometry of your platform’s hitbox using a polygon or series of vertices.

2. When a player (or other object) is within range of the platform’s hitbox, calculate the position of the player’s hitbox using a similar polygon/vertex system.

3. Use a collision detection algorithm (such as the Separating Axis Theorem) to detect if the hitboxes of the platform and player intersect.

4. If the hitboxes intersect, you can calculate the normal vector of the intersection area and use it to apply the appropriate physical forces to the player (e.g. bouncing off the platform, sliding along it, etc.) based on the angle and velocity of the player’s motion.

