To achieve this, you can modify the previous suggestions and follow these steps:

1. Add TPS rate to the User model

Edit the 'User' model (located at 'app/Models/User.php') and add a new 'tps_rate' field:

```php
protected $fillable = [
    'name', 'email', 'password', 'tps_rate',
];

// The 'tps_rate' column should also be added to the migration in 'database/migrations'

// Add a function to get the TPS rate per minute
public function tpsRatePerMinute()
{
    return $this->tps_rate * 60;
}
```

2. Create a custom Throttle middleware

Create a new middleware called 'CustomThrottleMiddleware.php' in 'app/Http/Middleware':

```php
namespace App\Http\Middleware;

use Closure;
use Illuminate\Http\Request;
use RuntimeException;
use Symfony\Component\HttpKernel\Exception\TooManyRequestsHttpException;

class CustomThrottleMiddleware
{
    public function handle(Request $request, Closure $next)
    {
        $user = $request->user();

        if (!$user) {
            throw new RuntimeException('User not authenticated');
        }

        $tpsRatePerMinute = $user->tpsRatePerMinute();

        // Set the custom throttle middleware to use the user's TPS rate per minute
        $response = $next($request);
        $response->headers->set('X-RateLimit-Limit', $tpsRatePerMinute);

        return $response;
    }
}
```

3. Register the custom middleware

Add the custom middleware to the 'routeMiddleware' array in 'app/Http/Kernel.php':

```php
protected $routeMiddleware = [
    // ...
    'customThrottle' => \App\Http\Middleware\CustomThrottleMiddleware::class,
];
```

4. Edit the API routes

Update 'routes/api.php' to use the custom Throttle middleware:

```php
Route::middleware(['auth:api', 'customThrottle'])->group(function () {
    Route::post('/service1', 'GatewayController@handleService1');
    Route::post('/service2', 'GatewayController@handleService2');
    // Add more routes for each service
});
```

5. Set permissions for each service

You can use Laravel's Gate and Policy for handling service permissions. First, define the Gates in the 'AuthServiceProvider' (located at 'app/Providers/AuthServiceProvider.php'):

```php
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Gate;

public function boot()
{
    $this->registerPolicies();

