I suggest refactoring your code with a new approach to avoid the use of `collectAsState` in this case. I have introduced a new composable, `FavoritesList`, which receives the list of favorite songs and passes it down to `AlbumDetailItem`. Here's the modified `FavoritesScreen` and the new `FavoritesList` composable:

```kotlin
@Composable
fun FavoritesScreen(navController: NavController) {
    val context = LocalContext.current
    val playerViewModel = viewModel<PlayerViewModel>(factory = PlayerViewModelFactory(context))
    val favorites by playerViewModel.favorites.collectAsState()

    Scaffold(
        topBar = { TopBar(title = "Favorites") },
        content = { padding ->
            Column(modifier = Modifier.padding(padding)) {
                FavoritesList(favorites, navController, playerViewModel)
            }
        }
    )
}

@Composable
fun FavoritesList(
    favorites: List<Song>,
    navController: NavController,
    playerViewModel: PlayerViewModel
) {
    LazyColumn {
        items(favorites.size) { index ->
            val song = favorites[index]
            AlbumDetailItem(song, navController, playerViewModel)
        }
    }
}
```

`FavoritesList` takes in the list of favorite songs, and then uses `items` in `LazyColumn` with the size of the list as the parameter. Inside that, it retrieves the specific song based on the index and passes it down to the `AlbumDetailItem`.

This approach should fix the type mismatch issue you were facing. Please update your `FavoritesScreen` and add `FavoritesList` composable accordingly.

