Below is an example of how to use PowerShell to run a particular test selection:

1. First, connect to the HLK Controller:

```powershell
$hpcController = New-Object -ComObject HpcScheduler.HpcClient
$controllerName = "YourControllerName"
$controllerPass = "YourControllerPassword"
$result = $hpcController.Connect($controllerName, $controllerPass, "HpcTask", $null)

if ($result) {
    Write-Host "Connected to HLK Controller"
} else {
    Write-Host "Failed to connect to HLK Controller"
    exit
}
```

2. Next, create a test selection based on a particular test:

```powershell
$productId = "YourProductId"
$selectionId = $hpcController.CreateTestSelection($productId, $null)

if ($selectionId) {
    Write-Host "Created test selection with ID: $selectionId"
} else {
    Write-Host "Failed to create test selection"
    exit
}
```

3. Now, find the sub-test to be run:

```powershell
$desiredSubTestName = "YourSubTestName"
$subTest = $hpcController.QueryDataTable("SELECT * FROM item WHERE parent=$selectionId AND criteriaName='$desiredSubTestName'")
```

4. After finding the sub-test, set it to 'Selected' status:

```powershell
if ($subTest.Rows) {
    $subTestId = $subTest.Rows[0]["id"]
    $hpcController.ChangeSelectionItemsState("item", $subTestId, "Selected")
    Write-Host "Selected sub-test: $desiredSubTestName"
} else {
    Write-Host "Failed to find sub-test: $desiredSubTestName"
    exit
}
```

5. Finally, run the test selection:

```powershell
$testResultId = $hpcController.RunSelection($selectionId)

if ($testResultId) {
    Write-Host "Running test selection with ID: $testResultId"
} else {
    Write-Host "Failed to run test selection"
    exit
}
```

