'locateChrome' is a deprecated Puppeteer method and is no longer available in the latest versions of Puppeteer. If you try to use this method, you may receive an error message stating that 'locateChrome' is not defined.

Instead, you can use the 'executablePath' option to specify the path to the Chrome or Chromium binary that you want Puppeteer to use. This will override the default path that Puppeteer uses to locate the Chrome or Chromium binary.

For example:
```javascript
const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');

(async () => {
  const browser = await puppeteer.launch({
    executablePath: '/path/to/chrome',
    headless: false,
  });
  const page = await browser.newPage();
  // do something with the page
  await browser.close();
})();
```

Make sure to replace '/path/to/chrome' with the actual path to your Chrome or Chromium binary.

