Please note that this example is a minimal implementation of an HTTP tunnel. To create a more robust and functional tunnel, consider implementing logic to handle retries, timeouts, and proper tunnel state management. Also, ensure that your server-side implementation processes the incoming POST requests appropriately, such as by forwarding the request data to the desired destination and sending back the correct responses.

