3. Use server-side functions like `reduceRegion()` or `reduceRegions()` to exploit Google Earth Engine's parallel processing capabilities. You can apply these functions on your ee.ImageCollection to find the mean or other statistics across a region of interest, which should significantly speed up your computations. You can find more information and code samples in the Earth Engine documentation [here](https://developers.google.com/earth-engine/guides/reducers_reduce_region).

